{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, as they journeyed from the east</b>. Rashi explained (Rashi on Genesis 11:2) that they were dwelling there, as is written above (Genesis 10:30), 'And their dwelling was from Mesha, as you go toward Sephar, the hill country of the east,' and they journeyed from there to seek for themselves a place that could sustain them, and they found only Shinar. But this is not correct, for the descendants of Shem alone are those concerning whom this is stated, and why would he attribute the dispersion to them, since the descendants of Japheth and the descendants of Ham were more numerous than they. Moreover, their dwelling in their lands was from Mesha to the hill country of the east, and the dispersion took place before they had that dwelling, for the descendants of Japheth did not come from the coastlands to the valley in the land of Shinar — rather, in the dispersion HaShem scattered them over the face of all the earth, and then they were settled in their lands, each to his nation. And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explained that Ararat is in the east, and he spoke well, for they are in the east near Assyria, as is stated (II Kings 19:37), 'and they escaped to the land of Ararat,' and Noah, when he descended from the mountain, settled in those lands, he and his descendants, and when they multiplied they journeyed from there to this valley. And the men of the dispersion, according to our Rabbis (Sanhedrin 109a), were rebelling against their Creator. And the pursuers of the plain sense (Ibn Ezra and Radak) say that their intention was only to be joined together, for Scripture stated their intention — 'lest we be scattered' — and did not report any other matter about them. But if according to their words they were foolish, for how could one city and one tower suffice for all the people of the world — or perhaps they thought that they would not be fruitful and would not multiply, and the seed of the wicked shall be cut off. But one who knows the meaning of 'a name' will understand their intention from what they said, 'let us make us a name,' and will know the extent of the plan they devised for the tower to build it, and will understand the entire matter — for they devised an evil scheme, and the punishment that came upon them to separate them into languages and lands was measure for measure, for they were cutting down the plantings. And behold, their sin resembles the sin of their father, and perhaps for this reason they expounded (Genesis Rabbah 38:9), 'which the children of men built' — Rabbi Berekhyah said: as the children of the masons, the children of the camel-drivers? Rather, the sons of the first man, etc. And observe that in the entire matter of the Flood, Scripture mentions Elohim, and in the entire matter of the dispersion, Scripture mentions the specific Name [YHWH], for the Flood was on account of the corruption of the earth, while the dispersion was on account of their cutting down the plantings — and they are punished by His great Name. And this is the reason for the descent, and likewise in the case of Sodom. And the enlightened will understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The closing phrase 'והמשכיל יבין' is a standard kabbalistic signoff; per instructions it is rendered literally and left cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:40.442619730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}